    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` field on the owner API following the existing evaluator-and-mapper pattern in the codebase.\n\n**The rule:** `riskFlag` is `true` when any of three soft signals hold \u2014 the owner is a possible duplicate, its email domain is disposable-adjacent, or its city is over its soft capacity \u2014 otherwise `false`.\n\nEach signal already had (or now has) a home, so no class became a catch-all:\n\n1. **Possible duplicate** \u2014 reused the existing `Owner.possibleDuplicate` flag set by `PossibleDuplicateDetector`.\n2. **City over soft capacity** \u2014 reused the existing `CityCapacityWarningEvaluator` (city holds 40\u201349 owners, the same \"approaching capacity\" threshold the `capacityWarning` field uses).\n3. **Disposable-adjacent email** \u2014 a new concept. Since the exact disposable domains are hard-rejected at create time by `DisposableEmailDomainValidator`, \"adjacent\" means the same provider *family* (a sibling TLD like `mailinator.net` or a subdomain like `inbox.mailinator.com`).\n\nNew/changed pieces:\n\n- **`DisposableEmailDomains`** \u2014 extracted the provider list and email/domain parsing into one shared component so the hard validator and the new soft check can't drift apart (removed the duplicated list + `domainOf` from `DisposableEmailDomainValidator`, which now delegates to it).\n- **`DisposableEmailDomainEvaluator`** \u2014 answers \"is this owner's email disposable-adjacent?\".\n- **`RiskFlagEvaluator`** \u2014 a thin composer that ORs the three signals; owns no signal logic itself.\n- **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 autowired `RiskFlagEvaluator` and added `@Mapping(target = \"riskFlag\", ...)`, mirroring how `capacityWarning`/`bulkSignupWarning` are mapped.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `riskFlag` boolean to the `OwnerDto` schema so the DTO getter/setter is generated.\n\nThe existing `coreRiskFlagFalseNormally` acceptance test (a plain owner returns `riskFlag: false`) passes.",
